[00:20.28]When the eyes of blind ones see again
[00:26.92]And the ears of deaf ones hear again,
[00:33.66]When the songs of children fill the air
[00:40.42]And joy and peace are ev’rywhere,
[00:47.10]When our loved ones will return to life,
[00:53.82]To an earth that’s free from sin and strife,
[01:00.35](Chorus)
[01:00.50]You will see how God these things supplies,
[01:09.04]If you keep your eyes on the prize.
[01:29.66]When the wolves and lambs will feed as one,
[01:36.16]When the bears and calves bask in the sun,
[01:42.90]Then a mere young boy will lead them all,
[01:49.66]And they will heed his childish call.
[01:56.46]When our tears belong to yesterday,
[02:03.20]When our fears and pain have passed away,
[02:09.36](Chorus)
[02:09.51]You will see how God these things supplies,
[02:21.40]If you keep your eyes on the prize.
